# Repo-only files (dev docs / DB scripts / deploy config) — belong in git, not
# served publicly. Pages deploys the whole repo since there's no build step,
# so these were reachable at yourdomain.com/<filename> with no auth. Blocking
# doesn't touch functions/, sitemap.xml, robots.txt, or any real page route.
# Trailing "!" forces the rule even though these are real files that exist in
# the deploy — without it Cloudflare lets the actual static file win.
/wrangler.toml /404.html 404!
/CLAUDE.md /404.html 404!
/HANDOVER.md /404.html 404!
/README.md /404.html 404!
/.gitignore /404.html 404!
/build/schema-d1.sql /404.html 404!
/build/seed-d1.sql /404.html 404!
